<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 16 June, from 1487 to 1976.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1487 CE <span class="tih-ago">539 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VII defeats the Yorkist rebels at Stoke Field</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry VII crushed a rebel army supporting the pretender Lambert Simnel. It is often counted as the last battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1779 CE <span class="tih-ago">247 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spain declares war on Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the American War of Independence, aiming to recover <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Minorca</a>. The Great Siege of Gibraltar that followed lasted more than three years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1858 CE <span class="tih-ago">168 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln delivers his 'House Divided' speech</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Accepting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> Republican nomination for the Senate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> warned that the nation could not endure 'permanently half slave and half free'. The speech raised his national profile.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1903 CE <span class="tih-ago">123 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ford Motor Company is incorporated</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry Ford and eleven investors founded the company in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detroit">Detroit</a>. Its Model T and moving assembly line made cars affordable to millions.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1963 CE <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Valentina Tereshkova becomes the first woman in space</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet cosmonaut Valentina Tereshkova launched aboard Vostok 6 and orbited Earth 48 times in nearly three days. No other woman flew in space for 19 years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1976 CE <span class="tih-ago">50 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Police fire on students in Soweto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Police shot at schoolchildren marching against compulsory <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaans">Afrikaans</a> teaching, killing 13-year-old Hector Pieterson among others. The uprising spread, and hundreds died in the months that followed.</p></div></li></ol>
